&lt;p&gt;Our customers include the world’s largest and most prominent healthcare systems, governments, retailers, restaurants and global businesses who rely on us to save lives, reduce emissions, increase economic opportunity, and provide delivery from point A to point B as fast as possible. The drone is only 15% of what we’ve built to enable seamless, reliable, global operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our system strengthens supply chains, reduces congestion, and gives people time back. With more than 140 million commercial autonomous miles safely flown, Zipline is redefining access to healthcare, consumer products, and food across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at a global scale and are looking for practical problem solvers who thrive on real-world challenges and rapid growth. Our team is motivated by building systems that have a direct, meaningful impact on people’s lives and by scaling the future of logistics. We are seeking people who sculpt from first principles, enjoy facing adversity, and can do the impossible at record breaking speeds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You and The Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ground Test Operators support the flight testing and operational validation of autonomous delivery aircraft in a high-tempo test environment. In this role, you will execute test procedures, prepare delivery packages, operate ground infrastructure, and coordinate closely with engineering, flight operations, and maintenance teams to ensure safe and reliable testing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ground Test Operators also support installation and servicing of Zipping Point Autokiosk systems, aircraft ground handling, and incident response operations. This role may include deployments to mobile or remote test sites to support field testing and large-scale operational campaigns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role would start as a Contract role with opportunity to convert into a full-time position.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role supports the execution and validation of operational testing for Zipline systems by preparing, labeling, and processing test packages for partner operational validation and loading them through automated kiosks and Zipping Point infrastructure. The position also involves safely moving Zip aircraft around the test site between docks, operational areas, and maintenance facilities, as well as installing, inspecting, and maintaining Zipping Point Autokiosk systems to ensure consistent operational readiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Team members in this role contribute to large-scale flight test campaigns that enable high-volume operational validation. They may support flight operations in capacities such as Visual Observer, Zipping Point Operator, or Technician, playing a critical role in ensuring safe, efficient, and reliable testing activities. The role may also require deployment to mobile platforms, including Ziplines mobile Test Site and other satellite test locations, to support distributed operational testing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additionally, this position is responsible for responding to operational incidents, including the recovery of aircraft or field equipment and assisting with safety containment procedures when required. Team members are expected to identify and document operational issues, collaborate with engineering teams to support troubleshooting efforts, and contribute to the continuous improvement of procedures, testing workflows, and operational documentation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and ability to follow operational procedures in a safety-critical environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work outdoors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work any shift and any day of the week to support continuous flight test operations&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in aviation, UAV operations, or flight test environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with autonomous systems or robotics platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating industrial or heavy equipment such as forklifts, lifts, or other machinery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience troubleshooting mechanical or operational systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Environment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work is performed in an active flight test environment, both indoors and outdoors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Role requires walking across large test areas and working around aircraft and ground equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift and move packages or operational equipment as part of daily work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work may involve operating or working around industrial equipment and heavy machinery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work may occur in all weather conditions, including heat, cold, wind, and rain, depending on testing requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to commercial sites &amp;amp; remote test sites may be required up to 30% of the time&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Else You Need to Know&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion or religious creed, mental or physical disability, medical condition, genetic information, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, military or veteran status, citizenship, or other characteristics protected by state, federal or local law or our other policies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value diversity at Zipline and welcome applications from those who are traditionally underrepresented in tech. If you like the sound of this position but are not sure if you are the perfect fit, please apply!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compensation: $22 - $26 / hour&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

abstractvc-alpaca:greenhouse:6002070004.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered self-clearing broker-dealer and brokerage infrastructure for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more. Our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://alpaca.markets/blog/alpaca-raises-150-million-at-a-1-15b-valuation-to-build-the-global-standard-for-brokerage-infrastructure/&quot;&gt;recent Series D funding round&lt;/a&gt; brought our total investment to over $320 million, fueling our ambitious vision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 9 million brokerage accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;opening financial services to everyone on the planet&lt;/strong&gt;. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by top-tier global investors, including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Unbound, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 380+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking a Lead Product Manager, Money Movement &amp;amp; Settlements to own Alpaca’s money-movement and settlements product area end-to-end - JIT funding, instant funding, post-trade settlement, prefunding, US and non-US funding rails, and the ancillary products that sit alongside (HY Cash, FPSL). This is a senior product role focused on area ownership and execution, not people management - you’ll own the area roadmap and personally ship across multiple lanes in parallel, partnering with the other PMs in the area to raise the standard of work shipped across the swimlane.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the intersection of regulated payments, post-trade settlement, and broker-as-a-service partner economics. You’ll unify what is today a set of important but fragmented initiatives - so partners get reliable, predictable money movement, settlement that scales, and clear documentation - while we expand globally across multiple licensed entities and regional payment rails. You’re expected to provide early signal on changing global payments frameworks rather than react after rules formalize.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work across many partner, engineering and operational teams, and you’ll represent the area in product reviews, partner exec syncs, and leadership-level discussions. Success is measured by partner adoption and production usage of money-movement and settlement capabilities - not by ship dates or volume of documentation alone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Things You Get To Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product vision, roadmap, and success metrics for the entire money-movement and settlements area - settlements (JIT, instant funding, post-trade, prefunding), funding rails (US and non-US ACH, wires, RTP, FedNow, regional rails), and ancillary products (HY Cash, FPSL).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personally execute across multiple in-flight lanes in parallel - not just sequencing them from above, but shipping work yourself on the most strategically important ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rationalize how we expose money-movement and settlement APIs and internal systems - including where a single settlement surface must flex for different partner operating models, geographies, and funding flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive build-vs-buy, partner-vs-direct, and onshore-vs-offshore tradeoffs across the area; re-sequence the roadmap under real constraints (regulator deadlines, partner asks, eng capacity).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner deeply with engineering, broker-dealer operations, treasury, compliance, legal, partnerships, success, and sales to prioritize initiatives that balance regulatory risk, operational load, revenue impact, and time-to-market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery with partners and prospects - understand blocking requirements, translate needs into sequenced roadmaps, push back on asks that don’t fit the platform, and communicate honest timelines and scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape pricing and packaging inputs where money-movement and settlement products imply different operational handling - working with commercial and treasury stakeholders so what we sell matches what we can deliver and support at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support global expansion of money-movement capabilities as Alpaca grows its regional broker-dealer footprint - including regional payment rails, FX corridors, and jurisdiction-specific rules (US / non-US).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and monitor adoption across the area - settlement success rate, time-to-funding, ACH return rate, instant-funding utilization, partner-reported blockers, operational throughput; willing to sunset or rework features that don’t drive adoption rather than calling them done at launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the standard of work shipped across the money-movement and settlements area - mentor peer PMs, set quality bar, unblock adjacent teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are (Must-Haves)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;10+ years of experience in Product Management, Engineering, Consulting, or starting a startup, with senior IC ownership in regulated payments, settlement, treasury, or brokerage clearing infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated end-to-end ownership of money-movement or settlement surfaces at production scale - at least two of: ACH / wire / RTP / FedNow rails, post-trade settlement, JIT or instant funding, prefunding, FX corridors, or broker-dealer clearing flows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Direct experience navigating US payments and clearing regulatory frameworks - NACHA ACH operating rules, Federal Reserve oversight, FINRA / SEC clearing and customer-protection rules, OFAC screening, AML / BSA obligations as they touch money movement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Track record of setting and executing an area-level roadmap across multiple in-flight workstreams in parallel - not just shipping a single product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proven ability to operate as a senior product owner who raises the standard around them - mentors peers, sets quality bar, represents the area in cross-functional and leadership forums without holding a manager title.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication; ability to run partner-facing conversations, regulator-adjacent forums, and internal leadership updates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience analyzing data using SQL and a relevant BI tool.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor’s degree in computer science, engineering, finance, or equivalent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll Thrive In This Role If You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excitement about growing your impact through scope and influence across the money-movement and settlements area, rather than through team size.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A track record of owning and shipping multiple workstreams in parallel over the last 2-3 years - not just setting vision and facilitating tradeoffs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on regulated-product experience at the shipping and mechanical-chain layer (e.g. ACH return code handling, settlement reconciliation, exception queues), not just the policy and framework layer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The senior posture to take over an in-flight money-movement and settlements roadmap from day one, without a six-month ramp.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Might Be (Nice-to-Haves)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Direct broker-dealer or institutional brokerage experience - Schwab, Fidelity, IBKR, Apex, Drivewealth, or correspondent-clearing equivalents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience standing up money-movement or settlement programs from scratch, not just iterating on inherited ones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with the B2B2C correspondent / broker-as-a-service model - partners as primary customers, end retail customers downstream.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Direct experience with DTCC, NSCC, Fedwire, or other clearing-house settlement flows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with global payment rails outside the US - SEPA, FPS, regional ACH equivalents, or stablecoin-rail funding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience unifying fragmented money-movement or settlement stacks behind consistent APIs and data models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Background in broker-dealer treasury or clearing operations (reconciliation, exception handling, regulatory reporting) and automation opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI-native PM workflow - recurring use of tools like Cursor, Claude, ChatGPT, NotebookLM, or custom agents in PRD drafting, customer-call synthesis, data exploration, and prototyping.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monthly Stipend: USD $150 per month via a Brex Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://files.alpaca.markets/disclosures/AlpacaRecruitmentPrivacyPolicy.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

