&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who are we?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sigmoid enables business transformation using data and analytics, leveraging real-time insights to make accurate and fast business decisions, by building modern data architectures using cloud and open source. Some of the world’s largest data producers engage with Sigmoid to solve complex business problems. Sigmoid brings deep expertise in data engineering, predictive analytics, artificial intelligence, and DataOps. Sigmoid has been recognized as one of the&amp;nbsp; fastest growing technology companies in North America, 2021, by Financial Times, Inc. 5000, and Deloitte Technology Fast 500.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Offices&lt;/strong&gt;: New York | Dallas | San Francisco | Lima | Bengaluru&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The below role is for our Bengaluru office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Sigmoid?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;Sigmoid provides the opportunity to push the boundaries of what is possible by seamlessly combining technical expertise and creativity to&amp;nbsp; tackle intrinsically complex business problems and convert them into straight-forward data solutions.&amp;nbsp;Despite being continuously challenged,&amp;nbsp; you are not alone. You will be part of a fast-paced diverse environment as a member of a high-performing team that works together to energize and inspire each other by challenging the status quo, Vibrant inclusive culture of mutual respect and fun through both work and play&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Management Consultant – Supply Chain &amp;amp; Manufacturing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(Management Consulting Team, India)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Roles and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own &amp;amp; drive execution of the business-analytics roadmap by demonstrating techno-functional consulting &amp;amp; stakeholder management capabilities in collaboration with data science &amp;amp; engineering SMEs and teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading client workshops where broad vision and ambiguous business problems are articulated &amp;nbsp; to be solved through data science and AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define business problems concisely, consolidate the findings and hypothesize the proposed solution. Measure and articulate how solutions and results improve clients’ objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently liaise with customers and convincingly present solutions in an unstructured and ever-changing client environment. Be able to independently question the customer, when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform a role that involves a combination of hands-on contribution, customer engagement &amp;nbsp; and team management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to organization building through training, mentoring, and developing repeatable analytic approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mandated Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s Degree (BE / BTech - CS) from Tier I / II universities like IIT’s / NIT’s and MBA from Top Tier B-schools (IIM) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-8 years of professional work experience in Supply Chain Analytics or SC Product Development, with at least 3 years spent delivering value for a Consumer Goods or Retail environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent research, analytical, and numerical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven exceptional problem-solving analytical skills with an ability to blend creativity and logical thought to innovatively think through a problem and develop solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop and articulate strategic recommendations based on rigorous data analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Should have developed new consulting business capabilities within&amp;nbsp; target Industry verticals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in strategy and business/technology consulting role conversant with process improvement, cost optimization, customer analytics and experience management, architecture assessments etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated sustained client relations management experience at a C-suite level or operated at a senior management level in the industry role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of applications of statistical and machine learning algorithms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management and team management skills and ability to work with global teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Any hands on quantitative experience with analytic tools&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing required inputs to sales, and pre-sales activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter who can work well with minimal guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote class=&quot;gmail_quote&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;By submitting your application, you consent to being contacted by our Talent Acquisition team via phone call, email, SMS, WhatsApp, or other communication channels regarding your application and relevant career opportunities.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

playground-saltbox:greenhouse:6014412004.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dock Sortation Specialist&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Operations · On-Site (Saltbox Location)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Saltbox is on a mission to simplify the hardest parts of running an eCommerce business. Our purpose-built spaces serve as modern headquarters for small to medium-sized businesses in industries like Fashion &amp;amp; Apparel, Health &amp;amp; Beauty, Electronics, and Household Goods. We offer a powerful combination of flexible warehouse suites, offices, and on-site logistics support that empower entrepreneurs to scale with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re launching something new at Saltbox—and we need the right people to run it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Dock Sortation Specialist, you’re the execution engine of our new Dock Sorting function. You’re on the floor every shift—scanning packages, sorting them accurately, staging them for drivers, and making sure every package gets where it needs to go, on time. This is a fast-paced, physical, detail-oriented role where accuracy and reliability aren’t just nice to have—they’re everything.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work alongside a small, tight-knit crew processing hundreds of packages per shift using handheld scanning technology. When the day is done, you may also pitch in to support other parts of the Saltbox operation—from member logistics to building upkeep—as part of our Elastic Workforce (e-Force). You’ll report to the Dock Sortation Lead at your location, with support from the Saltbox Operational Excellence team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Package Scanning &amp;amp; Sortation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scan every inbound package using the Sort App on a handheld device—each package gets two scans: presort and bin assignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a target scan rate of 225 scans per hour (approximately 112 packages processed per hour).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sort packages into the correct shelving unit or bin based on batch and market assignment. Accuracy is critical—missorts delay drivers and risk SLA breaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staging &amp;amp; Dispatch&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Move sorted batches to the driver handoff zone before the dispatch window opens.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with dispatch scanning as drivers pick up their loads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help ensure 99.5% of packages are dispatched by 11:00am.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driver Handoff &amp;amp; End-of-Shift Reconciliation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the Lead with driver coordination—staging packages for pickup, completing departure scans, and keeping the handoff zone organized.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help count on-hand packages at shift end and immediately flag any discrepancies to the Lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workspace Stewardship&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the sortation area clean, organized, and safe throughout your shift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Return equipment to proper positions and maintain the Saltbox standard for Members and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re reliable, detail-oriented, and take real pride in doing physical work well. You don’t need to be managed closely—you show up, you execute, and you hold yourself to a high standard. You’ll thrive here if you move with purpose, pay attention to the small details that matter, and bring a consistent, team-first attitude every shift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Qualities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dependable—your team can count on you being there, every shift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focused and purposeful in a fast-paced, high-volume environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented—right package, right bin, right scan, every time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with technology and quick to learn new tools and apps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works well on a team without needing constant direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Takes physical work seriously and can stay on your feet for a full shift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to stand for 6+ hours and lift/move packages up to 50 lbs (reasonable accommodation provided).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available for early morning shifts (typically 5:00am–1pm) on a rotating 7-day schedule with two consecutive days off. Shifts as early as 2:00am may be available as operations grow, with advance notice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliable transportation to your Saltbox location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using handheld scanning devices and mobile apps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in warehouse, logistics, fulfillment, or retail is a plus—but if you’ve got hustle, we’ll train you on everything else.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care deeply about our team and are proud to offer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance (100% covered for some plans, low premium for PPO)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K plan with options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-paid long and short-term disability insurance and life insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid holidays, vacation time, sick leave, and paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and development opportunities, including job training and a dedicated learning budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location &amp;amp; Schedule&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is on-site at the&lt;strong&gt; Alexandria, DC Saltbox &lt;/strong&gt;location. Shifts are early morning (typically 5:00am–1pm) on a rotating 7-day schedule, with two consecutive days off per week. As operations scale, shifts as early as 2:00am may be available. Only New Year’s Day and Christmas Day are closed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Are you ready to join a team that values your skills and experience? Saltbox is excited to offer this full-time position with a base pay range of $20.00–$22.00 per hour, depending on your location. We understand that the cost of living varies across different geographic markets, and we want to ensure that our compensation reflects that.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re looking for a role where showing up well and doing the work with care truly matters, we want to hear from you. Apply today and become a part of the Saltbox team!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re interested in learning more about Saltbox, check out our website: www.saltbox.com&lt;/p&gt;

qumracapital-jfrog:greenhouse:7565443.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate -- and we want you along for the ride. This is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit and just all-around great people. Here, if you’re willing to do more, your career can take off. And since software plays a central role in everyone’s lives, you’ll be part of an important mission. Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production -- a concept we call “liquid software.” Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us in our journey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Solution Engineer to be on the front lines, working closely with our customers and prospects, guiding them on how to build robust DevOps, DevSecOps and MLOps processes. You will work with our sales, product, customer success &amp;amp; engineering teams to help customers understand the value of JFrog Solution from a technical and business perspective. If you love working with brilliant people, being part of an energetic team and changing the world of software, you might be the perfect Frog to join our team!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Senior Solution Engineer in JFrog you will...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with enterprise customers to elevate their DevSecOps strategies and ensure they fully leverage the JFrog platform to enhance their software delivery pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with JFrog’s sales, product, customer success and engineering teams to drive successful technical win for sales opportunity and help customers realize true value of the solution by successful adoption.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage stakeholders and create champions by communicating the business value of JFrog’s solutions, demonstrating how JFrog solutions drive measurable business outcomes and empowering enterprise clients to make informed decisions for long-term success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical training sessions for our community and customers on DevSecOps best practices and the powerful capabilities of JFrog products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent JFrog at high-profile events and conferences, sharing insights and connecting with industry leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for the needs of enterprise customers, playing an essential role in shaping the JFrog product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously deepen your expertise in DevSecOps, MLOps, and the evolving technology landscape to bring cutting-edge insights to our clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a Senior Solution Engineer in JFrog you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7+ years in technical sales or sales engineering, with a proven track record of supporting enterprise software solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of FOSS, Docker, Kubernetes, CI servers, Git, Artifactory, SCA, SAST, IaS, MCP and other essential DevSecOps technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience with AWS, Azure, or GCP environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on experience in Linux or cloud infrastructure, critical for scaling solutions in complex enterprise environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience in leading and driving successful POC/POVs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the competitive landscape within Application Security and SDLC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer orientation with a proactive, &quot;can-do&quot; attitude and a relentless drive to learn and deliver impactful results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in software architecture design and large-scale product development is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills as well as customer presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenger mindset to discover improvised solutions for customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Value models / Value assessment is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT JFROG CAN OFFER…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At JFrog, base salary is only one component of our compensation package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position has a base salary range between $175,000 to $187,000. &amp;nbsp;Base salary will be based on your skills, qualifications, experience and location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additionally, this role may be eligible for discretionary bonuses or commission payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position also includes an equity package of restricted stock units (RSU). &amp;nbsp;In addition, JFrog employees are eligible to participate in our Employee Stock Purchase Plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JFrog provides employees comprehensive benefits including medical, dental, vision, retirement, wellness and much more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JFrog is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin or nationality, ancestry, age, disability, gender identity or expression, marital status or any other category protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;

